{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["צפנת פענח — as in its Targum, and it is the Egyptian language. And so was their practice, to call a person by an appropriate name at the time they appoint him over their house. And likewise: ויקרא משה להושע בן נון יהושע, when he became his attendant. And likewise: ויקרא לדניאל בלטשצר. As written: די שמיה בלטשצר כשם אלהי." "פוטיפרע — this is not Potiphar according to the plain sense." "כהן און — the official of that city, as written: ובני דוד כהנים היו שלטונים."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:03.255566890Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}